            "reviewer_id": "User_26448014_1_0",
            "review_title": "Review at Mawlana restaurant& cafe",
            "review_text": "emeisel w\n2 contributions\n0\nMemories to cherish for a Lifetime, the Legacy of Mawlana and it's founder, Ibrahim\nMay 2025 • Friends\nTruly the most heartwarming and absolutely phenomenal gateway to experiencing Middle-eastern and Mediterranean cuisine right around the expat thriving heart of Tay Ho, in Quang An. And turns out it's only here that authentic Egyptian gourmet dishes and desserts could be found, let's not forget the sprinkle of Syrian and Turkish delights served here alongside exquisite drinks. Calling this place, Mawlana, a restaurant or eaterie is a massive understatement. Walking through these doors feel enchanted like being teleported back to Egypt, and every single guest who walks in through these doors is sure to leave feeling a sense of belonging, warmth, hospitality and generosity that's going to stick with them throughout their lifetime and the Mastermind behind this magnificent establishment, is one of the most modest, kind and humble human beings to be gracing this planet, the one who makes it possible with his hard work day after day to bring smiles in the faces of wanderers with a backpack, families, couples, children, gentlemen, ladies and people from all walks of life alike, making sure to never let a guest who has walked through these doors leave, feeling unsatiated, and as if feeling like their heart isn't bursting out of gratitude and eyes getting teary out of pure joy and nostalgia with every single blood cell singing at the top of their lungs, with ecstasy and love... that Mastermind happens to be a dear brother of ours named Ibrahim, bless him and his family. There is absolutely nothing that can be criticized about the unwavering consistency in quality of the truly phenomenal Egyptian culinary delights and the ingredients are absolutely fresh as tasted, and served like a platter about to be presented Infront of Cleopatra herself. As for the size of portions per servings, there is no other place in my life that I've ever been that was as generous as brother Ibrahim here, and the portions served aren't filled with food alone but with the rarest treasure, the heart.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten June 22, 2025",
